What is left of the chaining gap. Release 9 adds `price_ore` by schema.sql
alone, NULL in every row. Release 10's step fills it: on a dev database,
long at release 9, it runs. Production is at release 8 and deploys 10
straight away: the steps run first, on the database as release 8 left it,
where no `price_ore` is yet. Refused, nothing changed (the rehearsal says
so before the deploy does). Deploying release 9 first, then 10, goes
through.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup', 95);

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL, price_ore INTEGER) STRICT;

== ledger
UPDATE dish SET price_ore = price_kr * 100;

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, price_kr INTEGER NOT NULL, price_ore INTEGER) STRICT;

